# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build products and environments — all regenerable by build_exe.ps1
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ffmpeg is downloaded automatically by build_exe.ps1 (~200 MB, and GitHub
# rejects files over 100 MB anyway).
launcher/bin/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Distribution channel. These are *outputs* of tools/publish_update.py, built
# from the source in this repo — committing them would version the same code
# twice and go stale the moment anything here changes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
updates/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data and results. Footage is large and belongs with the experiment, not the
# code; results are reproducible from the video plus a .rtcfg.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.MOV
*.mov
*.mp4
*.MP4
TestRun/
results/
out*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Kept on disk, out of the public repository.
#
# Neither is dead code and neither should be deleted locally:
#
#   tools/publish_update.py    builds every update payload and manifest, and is
#                              how patches reach an offline rig or a shared
#                              folder without a GitHub release.
#   tools/release-workflow.yml the source of .github/workflows/release-workflow.yml.
#                              That path is awkward to write to from tooling, so
#                              this copy is how workflow changes get delivered.
#   tests/                     the synthetic ground-truth harness. It generates a
#                              clip with prescribed length, frequency and
#                              occlusion, and scores the recovery against it --
#                              which is what every numerical change in this
#                              program has been checked with.
#
# They are excluded because the repository is the *application*, and someone
# cloning it to install the program has no use for either. Delete these two
# lines to publish them again.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/tests/
/tools/

# Local machine state
*.rtcfg
robotrack-selftest.log
robotrack-error.log
